WEBVTT

00:00.490 --> 00:03.679
<i> ♪  It seems today
that all you see  ♪ </i>

00:03.779 --> 00:07.048
 ♪  Is violence in movies
and sex on TV  ♪

00:07.082 --> 00:10.618
 ♪  But where are those
good old-fashioned values  ♪

00:10.652 --> 00:13.621
 ♪  On which we used to rely?  ♪

00:13.655 --> 00:17.124
 ♪  Lucky there's a family guy  ♪

00:17.159 --> 00:20.461
 ♪  Lucky there's a man
who positively can do  ♪

00:20.495 --> 00:22.063
 ♪  All the things that make us  ♪

00:22.097 --> 00:23.397
 ♪  Laugh and cry  ♪

00:23.432 --> 00:23.937
 ♪  He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy!  ♪

00:33.975 --> 00:36.610
<i>Aw, man, I've been dying
to see Maniac Pope 2.</i>

00:36.644 --> 00:37.945
The first one
was awesome.

00:37.979 --> 00:39.613
Is this one
of those theaters

00:39.647 --> 00:41.615
where they bring your beef stew
right to your seat?

00:41.649 --> 00:42.950
What? That's
not a thing.

00:42.984 --> 00:44.284
Sure is.

00:44.319 --> 00:47.154
Don't get mad at me 'cause
you don't know nothing fancy.

00:57.832 --> 00:59.466
I feel like I'm
being watched.

00:59.501 --> 01:01.135
Of course
you are, silly.

01:01.169 --> 01:03.170
The Lord is always
watching us.

01:14.749 --> 01:17.451
May the sword
be with you.

01:19.487 --> 01:21.955
And also with you!

01:21.990 --> 01:23.957
Geez, this movie sucks.

01:23.992 --> 01:25.292
I know,
it's terrible.

01:25.326 --> 01:26.960
Excuse me,
who had the stroganoff

01:26.995 --> 01:28.295
with the roasted
potatoes?

01:28.329 --> 01:29.730
Right here.

01:32.434 --> 01:35.135
Thank you for seeing me,
Your Excellency.

01:35.170 --> 01:36.303
Of course.

01:36.337 --> 01:38.238
What did you say your
name was, my child?

01:38.273 --> 01:40.841
Lucy.

01:41.776 --> 01:44.111
You've been "Lucified."

01:48.917 --> 01:50.217
That was awful.

01:50.251 --> 01:52.219
I know, they just redid
all the same stuff

01:52.253 --> 01:53.887
<i>from the first
Maniac Pope.</i>

01:53.922 --> 01:55.222
<i>Yeah, like in the first
Maniac Pope,</i>

01:55.256 --> 01:57.891
he says to Bruce,
"You've been Brucified."

01:57.926 --> 01:58.892
Like, that's
smart, right?

01:58.927 --> 02:00.227
That's a smart line.

02:00.261 --> 02:02.229
But he did the same thing
twice in this movie.

02:02.263 --> 02:04.898
Once to Lucy and once earlier
when he found that wild goose.

02:04.933 --> 02:06.300
It's just
bad writing.

02:06.334 --> 02:08.335
Yeah, I mean, we could write
a better horror movie than t Th.

02:08.369 --> 02:10.003
Really? You
think we could?

02:10.038 --> 02:13.974
Absolutely, I'm as creative as
the first spider to spin a web.

02:14.008 --> 02:15.642
Hey, you know how
we always dreamed

02:15.677 --> 02:17.644
about having a house
that comes out of our butts?

02:17.679 --> 02:18.679
Uh, what?

02:18.713 --> 02:19.680
Eh?

02:19.714 --> 02:20.681
Yeah.

02:20.715 --> 02:21.849
Butt-house.

02:26.654 --> 02:28.622
I found your cigarettes.

02:28.656 --> 02:30.290
That's all I'm gonna say.

02:30.325 --> 02:31.625
Morning, everybody.

02:31.659 --> 02:33.627
And the crisis
continues.

02:33.661 --> 02:34.628
What, these?

02:34.662 --> 02:35.629
Come on.

02:35.663 --> 02:37.631
Last thing I want
is attention.

02:37.665 --> 02:39.633
It's just that when you've
read as many books as I have,

02:39.667 --> 02:41.301
it-it takes a toll,
you know?

02:41.336 --> 02:42.636
You sure it's not
from watching

02:42.670 --> 02:44.638
too much close-up
porn on your phone?

02:44.672 --> 02:46.306
You know,
I wouldn't be surprised

02:46.341 --> 02:47.641
if they have that now.

02:47.675 --> 02:49.643
Brian, what do you
want for breakfast?

02:49.677 --> 02:51.011
Uh, hold on.

02:53.982 --> 02:56.617
What do I want?

02:56.651 --> 02:57.618
You're so full of it.

02:57.652 --> 02:58.952
You don't need
those things.

02:58.987 --> 03:00.621
Wait, who said that?

03:00.655 --> 03:01.955
Oh, Stewie.

03:01.990 --> 03:03.290
You are just horrible.

03:03.324 --> 03:04.625
You're even worse
than those people

03:04.659 --> 03:06.193
who take dumps
in the shower.

03:07.562 --> 03:08.529
What?

03:08.563 --> 03:09.863
W-Why are you cutting to me?

03:09.898 --> 03:11.198
What did somebody say?

03:11.232 --> 03:13.734
Whatever they said I do,
I don't do.

03:17.372 --> 03:19.673
All right, I got a
horror movie idea.

03:19.707 --> 03:21.174
<i>It's called
Cereal Killer.</i>

03:21.209 --> 03:24.745
A serial killer who only
kills people who eat cereal.

03:24.779 --> 03:27.414
Wait, what... what if God
is a serial killer?

03:27.448 --> 03:31.084
He lowers the average lifespan
of humans to 65,

03:31.119 --> 03:34.588
but there are many exceptions
based on genetics and diet.

03:34.622 --> 03:37.925
That's stupid-- I ain't never
heard of somebody lived to 65.

03:37.959 --> 03:39.927
Look, I think the problem is
this is a bar.

03:39.961 --> 03:41.261
We can't get
inspired here.

03:41.296 --> 03:42.729
We have to go someplace
scary, you know?

03:42.764 --> 03:44.064
To put us in the mood.

03:44.098 --> 03:46.533
I got it: the old Quahog Asylum.

03:46.568 --> 03:47.534
What?!

03:47.569 --> 03:48.702
We can't go there.

03:48.736 --> 03:50.370
That place has been
abandoned for years.

03:50.405 --> 03:52.706
And they say it's haunted
by a ghost with a hook-hand.

03:52.740 --> 03:54.374
That's why it's
the perfect place.

03:54.409 --> 03:55.709
If we want to write
a scary movie,

03:55.743 --> 03:57.044
we need to do it
somewhere scary.

03:57.078 --> 03:58.712
Well, I guess
we could try it.

03:58.746 --> 04:01.214
We have sort of just been
spinning our wheels here.

04:01.249 --> 04:02.549
No offense, Joe.

04:02.584 --> 04:04.551
I guess
Cleveland's right.

04:04.586 --> 04:06.553
So far, this has been
a bigger waste of time

04:06.588 --> 04:08.922
than an acceptance speech
at the Asperger's Awards.

04:08.957 --> 04:10.924
I'd like to thank
everyone I've ever met,

04:10.959 --> 04:13.260
in the order that I met them,
last name first,

04:13.294 --> 04:16.263
and if anyone interrupts me,
I'll have to start over.

04:31.613 --> 04:33.614
 ♪   ♪

04:49.097 --> 04:50.397
This place
is terrible.

04:50.431 --> 04:51.732
Are you kidding?

04:51.766 --> 04:53.367
It's the perfect place
to write a horror movie.

04:53.401 --> 04:54.701
All right, well,
I got an idea.

04:54.736 --> 04:56.036
You know, I like
them horror movies

04:56.070 --> 04:58.038
where you got a couple
of teenagers getting busy

04:58.072 --> 05:00.040
in their car
at Makeout Point,

05:00.074 --> 05:02.009
but there's a killer
on the loose.

05:07.782 --> 05:11.051
He Stacy, what do you say
we go all the way tonight?

05:11.085 --> 05:13.387
And then I unload
on the sun visors.

05:13.421 --> 05:15.055
Is that all
you ever think about?

05:15.089 --> 05:17.057
And besides, Richie,
aren't you worried

05:17.091 --> 05:19.593
about what the man on the radio
is saying right now?

05:19.627 --> 05:22.596
Another dead teenage couple
was found at Makeout Point,

05:22.630 --> 05:24.498
clawed beyond recognition.

05:24.532 --> 05:25.666
You see?

05:25.700 --> 05:27.334
There's a dangerous
creature out there.

05:27.368 --> 05:30.003
Oh, what, you mean the
big, rabid, slobbery cat

05:30.038 --> 05:31.672
what's been scratching
people to death?

05:31.706 --> 05:33.340
I don't believe
it exists, Stacy.

05:33.374 --> 05:35.676
Now, help me get the right
angle and lower the visor.

05:37.712 --> 05:39.012
Richie,
did you hear that?

05:39.047 --> 05:40.347
Will you calm down?

05:40.381 --> 05:41.682
We're the only
ones out here...

05:42.950 --> 05:44.418
Rrrawwwr!

05:47.055 --> 05:48.188
Oh, my God!

05:57.231 --> 05:59.266
<i>Wait, you were the guy
and the cat?</i>

05:59.300 --> 06:00.934
And what's with
that visor stuff?

06:00.968 --> 06:02.669
Did Richie achieve
release?

06:02.704 --> 06:04.004
Okay, of the three
of you,

06:04.038 --> 06:05.439
Cleveland's the only one
who gets it.

06:05.473 --> 06:07.441
That's an awful idea.
Well, I got one.

06:07.475 --> 06:09.643
We should write one
of them zombie movies

06:09.677 --> 06:12.312
where a guy wakes up in a
comfortable cotton hospital gown

06:12.346 --> 06:15.315
with the back open so there's
a nice breeze on your behind,

06:15.349 --> 06:17.317
and he's like, "This ain't bad."

06:17.351 --> 06:20.353
But then he notices
the hospital's empty.

06:25.393 --> 06:28.729
Nurse, I'm ready
for my sponge bath.

06:28.763 --> 06:30.397
Hmm.

06:30.431 --> 06:31.732
What happened to this place?

06:31.766 --> 06:33.366
Everybody up and gone.

06:38.706 --> 06:40.707
Hmm, that's annoying.

06:44.345 --> 06:46.646
Maybe it's a loose filament.

06:47.682 --> 06:50.183
Nope, that's a busted bulb.

06:53.387 --> 06:55.021
These are all 145s.

06:55.056 --> 06:56.423
I need a 180.

06:59.127 --> 07:01.795
Well, now, maybe I did
need a 145.

07:03.865 --> 07:05.732
There we go.

07:08.770 --> 07:11.271
Damn it, I guess
it's a wiring issue.

07:11.305 --> 07:12.606
That's it?

07:12.640 --> 07:14.441
What the hell? When do
the zombies show up?

07:14.475 --> 07:15.776
That's the thing.

07:15.810 --> 07:17.878
<i>Their shuttle was late.</i>

07:17.912 --> 07:19.546
I-I don't know,
I-I was thinking

07:19.580 --> 07:20.881
we'd write a movie
where something

07:20.915 --> 07:23.216
that's not supposed
to be scary becomes scary.

07:23.251 --> 07:24.551
Like an evil doll.

07:24.585 --> 07:26.887
Yeah, or-or like an
evil bar of soap.

07:26.921 --> 07:28.301
Peter, I don't think
that's such a good id...

07:28.325 --> 07:29.473
Too late.

07:32.660 --> 07:34.961
Oh, yeah, that's nice.

07:34.996 --> 07:38.565
Time to wash my body
with this harmless bar of soap.

07:43.337 --> 07:45.305
Hey, Ambassador Mumbasa,

07:45.339 --> 07:47.307
are you enjoying
that new soap I bought you

07:47.341 --> 07:48.975
from that mysterious Chinese man

07:49.010 --> 07:51.344
whose store was weirdly
not there the next day?

07:52.780 --> 07:54.414
Ambassador Mumbasa?

07:54.448 --> 07:57.918
Oh, my God, Ambassador Mumbasa!

08:09.330 --> 08:10.964
Ambassador Mumbasa?

08:10.998 --> 08:12.899
Assistant Ambassador Armstrong?

08:12.934 --> 08:14.601
Everything okay up there
with the bath?

08:31.519 --> 08:35.121
I wonder if everything's okay
up at the old embassy.

08:37.458 --> 08:39.759
All right, maybe coming here
wasn't such a great idea.

08:39.794 --> 08:41.428
Is anybody else getting
a little freaked out

08:41.462 --> 08:43.163
by all these
scary stories?

08:43.197 --> 08:45.599
Yeah, even my
spine is tingling.

08:45.633 --> 08:46.867
You guys, I'm scared.

08:46.901 --> 08:48.068
<i>You remember
that movie, The Blob?</i>

08:48.102 --> 08:49.269
What if the Blob?

08:49.303 --> 08:50.503
Let's get out of here.

08:52.807 --> 08:54.107
Aw, damn it, it's locked!

08:54.141 --> 08:56.109
Oh, my God, somebody
must have locked us in.

08:56.143 --> 08:57.777
We're gonna
die in here!

09:00.815 --> 09:03.116
Sorry, guys,
somebody e-mailed me a video

09:03.150 --> 09:04.718
of a sheep screaming.

09:12.694 --> 09:13.661
It was him.

09:13.695 --> 09:15.196
It was the hook-handed killer.

09:15.251 --> 09:16.918
He locked us in!

09:16.953 --> 09:18.887
All the windows
have bars on 'em.

09:18.921 --> 09:21.623
I think the only way out of here
is through this duct system.

09:21.658 --> 09:24.626
Guys, do the words
"dead by dawn" scrawled

09:24.661 --> 09:26.962
in feces over there
mean we're in trouble?

09:26.996 --> 09:28.296
Did you do it?
I did.

09:28.331 --> 09:29.464
Then no.

09:34.337 --> 09:36.638
Still sticking with
the glasses, huh?

09:36.673 --> 09:37.639
What? Oh, right.

09:37.674 --> 09:39.307
Right,
I have glasses.

09:39.342 --> 09:41.309
They're such a part of me now,
I-I forgot all about 'em.

09:41.344 --> 09:42.644
You're gross.

09:43.281 --> 09:44.581
You know, it's funny,

09:44.615 --> 09:47.317
I-I've gotten an awful
lot of writing done

09:47.351 --> 09:49.319
You're a writer?

09:49.353 --> 09:51.321
I-I like to consider
myself an observer.

09:51.355 --> 09:53.323
You have nice
breasts, for instance.

09:53.357 --> 09:55.325
You want to join me?

09:55.359 --> 09:56.993
Guy with glasses
can't be all bad.

09:57.028 --> 09:58.328
Thanks.

09:58.362 --> 09:59.996
Boy, it's loud
in here, huh?

10:00.031 --> 10:03.099
Wh-When they said "Professor
Griffin," I barely heard them.

10:03.134 --> 10:05.135
That's it, I'm putting
an end to this.

10:05.169 --> 10:08.004
I'm gonna destroy those glasses
if it's the last thing I do.

10:08.039 --> 10:09.673
You should
really check out

10:09.707 --> 10:12.375
the Thanksgiving jazz
CD they sell here.

10:23.187 --> 10:24.788
Where the hell are we?

10:26.490 --> 10:27.657
I heard something.

10:27.692 --> 10:29.326
Is... is someone else here?

10:29.360 --> 10:30.994
Oh, my God,
it's Hook-hand!

10:31.028 --> 10:32.429
He's coming for us!

10:32.463 --> 10:34.431
Damn it, why can't
I get any reception?

10:34.465 --> 10:36.766
Because we're in a basement
in the middle of nowhere.

10:36.801 --> 10:38.435
Besides,
if cell phones worked,

10:38.469 --> 10:40.103
every movie would be
two minutes long.

10:40.137 --> 10:41.771
<i>Like An Affair
to Remember.</i>

10:45.376 --> 10:48.345
 ♪   ♪

10:48.379 --> 10:51.014
Darling, I was running
to the Empire State Building

10:51.048 --> 10:53.350
to see you,
but I got hit by a car.

10:53.384 --> 10:54.484
No wonder you were late.

10:54.518 --> 10:55.485
I'll be right down.

10:55.519 --> 10:56.486
Are you okay?

10:56.520 --> 10:58.722
I think I may be paralyzed.

10:58.756 --> 11:00.924
I'm sorry, there's nobody here
by that name.

11:02.259 --> 11:04.260
 ♪   ♪

11:11.035 --> 11:13.203
Wow, Stewie, thanks for
taking me to the spa.

11:13.237 --> 11:14.804
Hey, you deserve
it, buddy.

11:14.839 --> 11:17.240
So just relax, take
your glasses off,

11:17.274 --> 11:19.075
take a nice,
dry sauna--

11:19.110 --> 11:20.377
no glasses in
the sauna--

11:20.411 --> 11:21.611
just leave those
puppies in the locker.

11:21.645 --> 11:22.812
They'll be safe
out here.

11:22.847 --> 11:24.647
Sounds good.

11:32.690 --> 11:33.656
Come on, Chris.

11:33.691 --> 11:34.691
Don't let me down.

11:34.725 --> 11:36.059
Don't worry, Stewie.

11:36.093 --> 11:37.060
Chris!

11:37.094 --> 11:38.061
What are you
doing in here?

11:38.095 --> 11:39.195
I did it.

11:39.230 --> 11:40.563
I locked us in the sauna!

11:40.598 --> 11:41.564
You what?!

11:41.599 --> 11:42.966
Yep, it's all set.

11:43.000 --> 11:44.134
It's turned up high,

11:44.168 --> 11:47.170
and nobody is coming
for the whole weekend.

11:53.744 --> 11:56.513
Boy, you guys sure
look steamed.

11:56.547 --> 11:58.948
<i>This Family Guy joke was
written by Jimmy Sullivan,</i>

11:58.983 --> 12:01.050
<i>age nine, of Decatur, Georgia.</i>

12:01.085 --> 12:02.619
<i>Thanks, Jimmy!</i>

12:02.653 --> 12:05.688
<i>And we'll pass along your
gross request to Mila Kunis.</i>

12:13.898 --> 12:15.765
Those footsteps
are getting closer.

12:15.800 --> 12:16.866
Those aren't footsteps.

12:16.901 --> 12:18.568
It's an old building.
Just relax.

12:18.602 --> 12:20.303
Besides, I can see an exit door
right there.

12:20.337 --> 12:21.838
Where?
Right there.

12:21.872 --> 12:23.039
Behind that guy with the hook--

12:29.814 --> 12:31.481
Everybody run!

12:41.625 --> 12:42.959
Wait a minute.

12:42.993 --> 12:44.794
There's four of us,
and one of him.

12:44.829 --> 12:46.596
Yeah, let's
get him!

12:50.201 --> 12:51.634
Son of a bitch!
Take that!

12:51.669 --> 12:53.570
Die, Hook-hand!
You won't kill us!

12:58.275 --> 13:01.010
Um, Hook-hand's name is Albert,

13:01.045 --> 13:02.612
and he's dressed like a janitor.

13:02.646 --> 13:04.514
I've been...

13:04.548 --> 13:06.049
trying to help you.

13:06.083 --> 13:08.685
I'm the caretaker here.

13:08.719 --> 13:09.953
Wait, you work here?

13:09.987 --> 13:11.187
But you have
a hook hand.

13:11.222 --> 13:12.856
I was a soldier.

13:12.890 --> 13:16.459
I lost my hand
saving six men in Korea.

13:16.494 --> 13:18.661
Oh, God, he's
a war hero.

13:20.798 --> 13:22.365
He's dead.

13:22.433 --> 13:23.700
What have we done?

13:23.734 --> 13:25.869
We killed
an innocent man.

13:30.441 --> 13:33.877
Well, if this doesn't justify
a McFlurry, nothing does.

13:42.290 --> 13:45.192
Oh, my God,
we killed an innocent man.

13:45.226 --> 13:46.693
We-we've got
to report this!

13:46.728 --> 13:48.061
We gotta turn
ourselves in!

13:48.096 --> 13:49.229
No way.

13:49.264 --> 13:50.864
If we do that,
we'll all go to jail.

13:50.898 --> 13:52.065
And I'm a cop.

13:52.100 --> 13:54.067
Do you know what they
do to cops in jail?

13:54.102 --> 13:55.168
Hey, man?

13:55.203 --> 13:56.503
When you were
a cop, did they--

13:56.537 --> 13:57.938
did they let you
use the siren?

13:57.972 --> 13:59.740
Yeah, it's part
of the job.

13:59.774 --> 14:00.741
That's so cool!

14:00.775 --> 14:01.842
Hey, hey, when
you were a cop,

14:01.876 --> 14:03.076
when you were going
to a crime scene,

14:03.111 --> 14:05.145
<i>did you go "chung Chung,"
like Law & Order?</i>

14:05.179 --> 14:06.947
No, that would be
very unprofessional.

14:06.981 --> 14:08.215
All right,
all right.

14:08.249 --> 14:10.183
Oh, hey, check it out,
man, when you were a cop,

14:10.218 --> 14:12.185
did you ever, you know,
use your handcuffs

14:12.220 --> 14:14.121
when you were getting
kinky with your girl?

14:14.155 --> 14:15.355
No, it's city property,

14:15.390 --> 14:17.057
so you're not really
supposed to take those home.

14:17.091 --> 14:18.191
Oh, for sure, for sure.

14:18.226 --> 14:19.393
Oh, hey, by the way,

14:19.427 --> 14:21.728
a bunch of us are gonna kill
you in the shower later.

14:25.500 --> 14:27.934
Okay, so we're all on
the same page, right?

14:27.969 --> 14:29.169
We bury the body,

14:29.203 --> 14:30.570
we never speak
of this again.

14:30.605 --> 14:32.372
Deal. - Got it.
Yup.

14:39.147 --> 14:41.815
Wow, that was exhausting.

14:41.849 --> 14:44.117
Wait a minute, is-is that--
is that his car?

14:56.998 --> 14:58.632
Aw, crap, it's still alive!

15:08.076 --> 15:11.411
It does not feel
like a Wednesday.

15:17.151 --> 15:19.219
Peter, I'm glad
you're up.

15:19.253 --> 15:21.355
I need to talk to you
about something.

15:21.389 --> 15:23.390
I know what you did
last night.

15:24.525 --> 15:25.692
You do?

15:25.727 --> 15:28.061
How could you do
something so heinous?

15:28.096 --> 15:30.263
Last night,

15:30.298 --> 15:32.199
you left your dirty dishes
in the sink.

15:32.233 --> 15:34.434
It's disgusting.

15:34.469 --> 15:37.270
So I did half, and I left
the other half for you.

15:38.973 --> 15:39.973
Ah, forget it.

15:40.007 --> 15:40.974
You'll just do it wrong.

15:41.008 --> 15:42.209
I'll wash 'em myself.

15:42.243 --> 15:44.378
Why don't you just go
in the other room and relax?

15:44.412 --> 15:46.079
I'll call you
when breakfast is ready.

15:46.114 --> 15:47.347
Okay.

15:48.916 --> 15:51.151
Oh, my God, Peter,
come look at the newspaper!

15:51.185 --> 15:52.652
"Janitor dead."

15:53.521 --> 15:54.788
What? No!

15:54.822 --> 15:57.791
Right here.
My college roommate, Jan Itter.

15:57.825 --> 15:59.926
She passed away yesterday.

15:59.961 --> 16:01.361
Are-are we really
doin' this?

16:01.396 --> 16:03.130
'Cause I didn't get, like,
any sleep last night.

16:03.164 --> 16:04.598
What are you
freaking out about?

16:04.632 --> 16:05.999
You didn't even know her.

16:06.033 --> 16:08.101
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
y-you're right, you're right.

16:09.670 --> 16:12.205
You and the guys
killed and buried a man?!

16:12.240 --> 16:13.907
Ah, I knew
you'd find out!

16:13.941 --> 16:15.575
Find out what?

16:15.610 --> 16:16.910
I just got
David Sedaris' new book,

16:16.944 --> 16:19.212
<i>You and the Guys Killed
and Buried a Man.</i>

16:19.247 --> 16:20.881
Okay, I am
really on edge

16:20.915 --> 16:23.049
and this thing we're doin',
I'm not happy about it,

16:23.084 --> 16:25.385
and that's a very odd title
for a humorist's book.

16:25.420 --> 16:26.720
Peter, you're acting
very weird.

16:26.754 --> 16:27.854
Just go in
the other room.

16:27.889 --> 16:29.356
I don't want to go
in the other room,

16:29.390 --> 16:31.358
I want to stay here and
see what you're seeing,

16:31.392 --> 16:33.560
because you're saying
things that I think are

16:33.594 --> 16:35.262
somethin' totally different
than what they are.

16:35.296 --> 16:37.030
Peter, you're gonna
have a heart attack.

16:37.064 --> 16:40.434
I won't say anything,
I'll let you relax.

16:41.669 --> 16:43.503
"They found a body
of a war hero

16:43.538 --> 16:45.338
down by the old asylum!"

16:45.373 --> 16:47.207
Okay, that has to be something.

16:47.241 --> 16:48.742
Oh, sorry, Peter,

16:48.776 --> 16:52.446
I'm just singing along with
this old John Mellencamp song.

16:52.480 --> 16:56.817
 ♪  They went up there
to write a movie  ♪

16:56.851 --> 17:00.821
 ♪  Peter, Quagmire,
Cleveland and Joe  ♪

17:00.855 --> 17:04.024
 ♪  Killed the old janitor
war hero  ♪

17:04.058 --> 17:07.060
 ♪  Just why, we'll never know  ♪

17:07.094 --> 17:08.562
I don't remember
this one.

17:08.596 --> 17:11.031
Guess it's never been
in a car commercial.

17:11.065 --> 17:14.267
 ♪  In a truck
that's built Dodge Tough!  ♪

17:14.302 --> 17:15.902
Oh, yeah, no,
I know this one.

17:23.511 --> 17:24.644
Hey, Bri?

17:24.679 --> 17:27.180
Yeah? Aah!
Damn it! Aah!

17:27.215 --> 17:28.748
There's glass in my eye!

17:28.783 --> 17:30.417
Oh! Son of a bitch!

17:30.451 --> 17:31.751
Aah!

17:31.786 --> 17:33.186
Mom says dinner's at 6:00.

17:33.221 --> 17:35.956
She wanted me to tell people,
I don't know why.

17:41.529 --> 17:44.798
Guys, I'm kind of freaking out
about killing that guy.

17:44.832 --> 17:47.033
Anybody else have
a hard time sleeping?

17:47.068 --> 17:49.035
No, but there's an old
John Mellencamp song

17:49.070 --> 17:50.770
you're not gonna
believe.

17:50.805 --> 17:51.938
Wait, w-what's
all this stuff

17:51.973 --> 17:53.406
about you guys
killing someone?

17:53.441 --> 17:54.841
Last night,
at the asylum.

17:54.876 --> 17:55.909
We killed
that war hero.

17:55.943 --> 17:57.077
Whoa, whoa, what?!

17:57.111 --> 17:58.712
You-you really
killed someone?

17:58.746 --> 18:01.147
Holy moly, I don't think
I want to hear this.

18:01.182 --> 18:03.083
Quagmire, you were
there with us.

18:03.117 --> 18:04.417
You're so weird.

18:04.452 --> 18:05.785
Last night, I was
in St. Louis.

18:05.820 --> 18:07.053
I even have
a picture.

18:07.088 --> 18:08.355
See that?

18:08.389 --> 18:09.723
That's yesterday's date
on that newspaper.

18:09.757 --> 18:11.191
<i>On The Quahog Informant?</i>

18:11.225 --> 18:14.160
<i>They sell The Quahog
Informant in St. Louis?</i>

18:14.195 --> 18:15.829
Well, probably, but good
luck with that whole

18:15.863 --> 18:18.732
"you three and not me
killed a guy" thing.

18:18.766 --> 18:20.634
Damn it, that bastard
is bailing on us.

18:20.668 --> 18:23.637
He's a worse accomplice
than Johnny Wind Chimes.

18:26.007 --> 18:27.240
Hey! Shh!

18:27.275 --> 18:28.341
Sorry!

18:28.376 --> 18:29.976
It's my chimes.

18:38.452 --> 18:40.654
I hate to frame you like this,
Quagmire, but I gotta.

18:40.688 --> 18:42.088
I can't go to jail!

18:42.123 --> 18:44.558
They'll razz me good
on account of my belly.

18:48.596 --> 18:50.030
Cleveland?

18:50.064 --> 18:51.064
What are you
doing here?

18:51.098 --> 18:52.499
What are you
both doing here?

18:52.533 --> 18:54.301
Joe?
What the hell?

18:54.335 --> 18:55.702
You backstabbers.

18:57.405 --> 18:59.205
What the hell's
going on?

18:59.240 --> 19:00.473
I'll tell you
what's going on.

19:00.508 --> 19:02.142
Cleveland's tryin' to frame me.

19:02.176 --> 19:04.544
He's got my miniature
portraits of cool guys.

19:04.579 --> 19:06.179
Peter, those are baseball cards.

19:06.213 --> 19:08.315
Whatever. He's using it
to frame me for murder!

19:08.349 --> 19:09.916
Well, I'm not
the only one.

19:09.951 --> 19:12.819
<i>Joe's got my Sports Illustrated
football phone.</i>

19:12.853 --> 19:15.689
He was using this
as his main phone.

19:15.723 --> 19:17.324
It is a mess over there.

19:17.358 --> 19:18.892
Look at all
you pathetic people,

19:18.926 --> 19:20.393
bringing stuff
to frame each other.

19:20.428 --> 19:21.728
You're supposed
to be friends.

19:21.762 --> 19:23.163
Hey, that's
my shovel!

19:23.197 --> 19:24.164
Damn right!

19:24.198 --> 19:25.165
That's how smart I am,

19:25.199 --> 19:26.433
I only had to bring one thing!

19:26.467 --> 19:28.568
This way I can dig the hole
and just throw this in!

19:28.603 --> 19:29.936
But once you throw
it in there,

19:29.971 --> 19:31.838
how you gonna get
the dirt back on top?

19:31.872 --> 19:34.007
Give me your shovel!

19:34.041 --> 19:35.675
You're gonna have
to kill me first!

19:35.710 --> 19:37.744
Not with my shovel!
That's brand-new!

19:37.778 --> 19:40.080
Give me back
my rattle-y plastic phone!

19:40.114 --> 19:42.582
 ♪   ♪

19:48.789 --> 19:50.457
Wait, wait, wait, guys! Guys!

19:50.491 --> 19:51.124
What?

19:51.158 --> 19:52.359
Don't you see?

19:52.393 --> 19:53.393
This!

19:53.427 --> 19:55.428
This is our horror movie!

20:03.004 --> 20:04.971
 ♪   ♪

20:16.017 --> 20:19.953
It doesn't feel
like a Wednesday.

20:23.290 --> 20:24.357
Boy, that sucked.

20:24.392 --> 20:25.692
Yeah, I guess writing a movie

20:25.726 --> 20:27.694
isn't as easy as Joseph
Gordon-Levitt makes it look.

20:27.728 --> 20:29.396
Hey, at least
we gave it a shot.

20:29.430 --> 20:31.598
I just feel bad
we killed an innocent man.

20:31.632 --> 20:33.366
Well, don't feel too bad.

20:33.401 --> 20:34.401
Look at that!

20:38.673 --> 20:39.906
Oh, my God!

20:39.940 --> 20:41.541
Wow, that's a relief!

20:41.575 --> 20:43.777
We may have actually made
this town a better place.

20:43.811 --> 20:45.145
Yeah, what a monster.

20:45.179 --> 20:47.414
But at least now
he's gone forever.

20:47.448 --> 20:53.948
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru